  "prefix_and_root_conditions": {
    "unit": "The targeted n is that of the inner preverb ni. The r which triggers the change belongs to the outer pra/pari. The ordered action/prefix relation and one of the five quoted lexical roots are premises.",
    "nad": "The grammatical example has praṇinadati and pariṇinadati: the lexical first n is dental. Retain it separately from the retroflex of the inner prefix.",
    "sham": "The Padamañjarī identifies the śyan lengthening of śamām aṣṭānām. This is 04.0098 “be quiet”. The two PG209 causative sense profiles and 10.0218 curādi ālocana have other factors. Their selection under the residual rule would require its own analysis.",
    "augmented": "aṭ of laṅ is after the inner prefix. The intervening augment is expressly admitted at 8.4.17; final i of ni gives y before a. The transmitted controls are praṇyagadat and pariṇyagadat.",
    "excluded_readings": "Tattvabodhinī expressly excludes intensive yaṅ-luk under the citation form, e.g. the prefix n in pranijāgadīti. Padamañjarī separately discusses the third preverb upa in pranyupagadati. These examples do not turn into extra licensed spellings in the simple grid."
  },
